1
00:01:30,410 --> 00:01:34,979
[AWAKEN]

2
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:37,950
[Episode 12]

3
00:02:09,470 --> 00:02:10,800
What's wrong, Grandma?

4
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:14,590
Remember,

5
00:02:15,390 --> 00:02:17,230
your father is gone.

6
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:22,630
Three bullets from the Japanese
are still lodged in his body.

7
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:24,180
Don't cry!

8
00:02:24,210 --> 00:02:24,910
Grandma isn't crying,

9
00:02:24,910 --> 00:02:26,110
so we mustn't either!

10
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,279
Stop pretending.

11
00:04:17,269 --> 00:04:19,329
Never seen a woman in pajamas before?

12
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:20,800
I have.

13
00:04:21,950 --> 00:04:24,210
In the pajama ads of Wanxiang Pictorial.

14
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:27,240
How about I take a picture of you too

15
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:29,500
and put it in the studio window tomorrow?

16
00:04:35,659 --> 00:04:36,520
Don't you dare.

17
00:04:48,430 --> 00:04:49,240
I'm so cold.

18
00:04:50,630 --> 00:04:52,430
Should I get you a blanket, then?

19
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:55,680
Or...

20
00:04:56,310 --> 00:04:57,550
a hot water bottle?

21
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:00,020
I don't want a blanket.

22
00:05:01,510 --> 00:05:03,170
A blanket isn't as warm as you.

23
00:05:05,950 --> 00:05:06,830
Rascal,

24
00:05:08,510 --> 00:05:10,910
we came all the way
from Hangzhou together,

25
00:05:12,190 --> 00:05:13,920
and now we've become a family.

26
00:05:16,070 --> 00:05:17,130
Don't you think...

27
00:05:18,950 --> 00:05:20,260
that's a kind of fate?

28
00:05:21,750 --> 00:05:23,000
I guess it is.

29
00:05:25,070 --> 00:05:27,000
But can you get off me first?

30
00:05:28,710 --> 00:05:29,880
I don't want to.

31
00:05:30,430 --> 00:05:31,310
Quit it.

32
00:05:31,330 --> 00:05:33,530
You're not a monkey hanging from a tree.

33
00:05:37,630 --> 00:05:38,630
You're

34
00:05:40,070 --> 00:05:42,200
the only one I want to fool around with.

35
00:05:49,750 --> 00:05:51,810
I see the photos have been developed.

36
00:06:09,950 --> 00:06:10,950
This one is good.

37
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,160
When I die,

38
00:06:15,630 --> 00:06:17,070
remember to put this one

39
00:06:17,430 --> 00:06:18,720
on my tombstone.

40
00:06:21,190 --> 00:06:22,650
You won't die that easily.

41
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:32,270
We can't go to

42
00:06:33,159 --> 00:06:34,620
the MGM ballroom anymore.

43
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:38,980
Someone just started shooting
out of nowhere.

44
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:40,600
In the future,

45
00:06:41,409 --> 00:06:43,470
we'll have to find another ballroom.

46
00:06:45,870 --> 00:06:47,800
Where did you go after the incident

47
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:49,290
at the ballroom?

48
00:06:49,930 --> 00:06:51,659
I got out of there immediately.

49
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:53,120
What else could I do?

50
00:06:53,730 --> 00:06:55,460
Stay there and wait to get shot?

51
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:24,760
You should be an actress.

52
00:07:27,890 --> 00:07:29,750
You're wasted as a dance hostess.

53
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:44,900
Are you going to eliminate me too?

54
00:07:53,390 --> 00:07:54,560
Then do it.

55
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:59,040
Does anyone else know?

56
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:02,830
How would I know?

57
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:10,140
Then let me ask it another way.

58
00:08:11,750 --> 00:08:13,340
Will you tell Du Huangqiao?

59
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,240
You're family.

60
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:24,160
I won't hurt you.

61
00:08:31,950 --> 00:08:32,750
Are you crazy?

62
00:08:36,669 --> 00:08:38,340
I knew you loved me.

63
00:08:39,950 --> 00:08:41,150
Go away. G-Get off me!

64
00:08:41,549 --> 00:08:43,320
Can't you be serious, even now?

65
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:46,260
You don't look like
someone from the NBIS at all.

66
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:51,800
When I was very young,

67
00:08:53,030 --> 00:08:54,760
I was separated from my family.

68
00:09:01,110 --> 00:09:02,440
-Jinbao!
-Sister!

69
00:09:02,470 --> 00:09:03,590
-Jinbao!
-Sister!

70
00:09:02,940 --> 00:09:03,600
[Manchukuo National Defense
Women's Association]

71
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:05,480
-Jinbao!
-Sister!

72
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,320
The Manchukuo National Defense
Women's Association

73
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:10,120
was just a prostitution ring.

74
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,720
My first man,

75
00:09:14,260 --> 00:09:15,380
Kitahara Sosuke—

76
00:09:15,940 --> 00:09:19,470
without him, the dance hall queen
you see today wouldn't exist.

77
00:09:24,390 --> 00:09:26,390
I played the role of his wife.

78
00:09:27,150 --> 00:09:28,270
My only goal

79
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:30,120
was to escape.

80
00:09:31,930 --> 00:09:33,010
It was then

81
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:36,980
that I met the person
who recruited me into the NBIS.

82
00:09:38,870 --> 00:09:40,870
During the time I was away from home,

83
00:09:41,630 --> 00:09:43,960
my father was taken away and conscripted.

84
00:09:44,810 --> 00:09:46,070
My grandmother told me

85
00:09:47,390 --> 00:09:49,000
the Japanese had left 3 bullets

86
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,640
in my father's body,

87
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:53,970
and they threw his body
onto a heap of corpses.

88
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:55,150
After that,

89
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:58,960
I officially joined the NBIS.

90
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:01,050
[Zheng Jiaxun, NBIS Agent]

91
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:12,620
ID, please.

92
00:10:14,910 --> 00:10:15,710
Open the door!

93
00:10:28,950 --> 00:10:31,280
You're the real God of Wealth, aren't you?

94
00:10:31,910 --> 00:10:33,640
Auntie was just your stand-in.

95
00:10:35,670 --> 00:10:37,670
That was arranged by our superiors.

96
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:40,200
She didn't know my identity either.

97
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:46,760
I've told you my most important secret.

98
00:10:47,590 --> 00:10:50,120
Now you should
stop hiding things from me too.

99
00:10:53,630 --> 00:10:54,560
What am I hiding?

100
00:10:57,750 --> 00:10:59,880
What exactly do you want me to tell you?

101
00:11:01,100 --> 00:11:04,230
You didn't just start
suspecting me yesterday, did you?

102
00:11:09,550 --> 00:11:10,840
Ever since you said

103
00:11:11,570 --> 00:11:15,280
the gun used to shoot Hoshino
at the racecourse was a spring-loaded gun,

104
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:16,470
I've had my doubts.

105
00:11:18,150 --> 00:11:18,870
Why?

106
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:23,440
You said you saw that gun

107
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:24,480
in The Detective.

108
00:11:25,550 --> 00:11:27,000
But The Detective

109
00:11:27,390 --> 00:11:28,920
has never featured that gun

110
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:31,150
since its first issue.

111
00:11:32,640 --> 00:11:34,440
You went through that magazine?

112
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:38,740
I was looking for a weapon that suited me.

113
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:41,930
I didn't expect you to lie to me.

114
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:45,080
How adorable.

115
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:47,510
Besides you,

116
00:11:47,910 --> 00:11:50,170
no one else would do something like that.

117
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:54,250
You should be more careful from now on.

118
00:11:54,510 --> 00:11:55,970
This bouquet of lilies...

119
00:11:56,950 --> 00:11:59,150
Young Master Feng gave it to you, right?

120
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:05,570
You seem more like
a secret agent than I do.

121
00:12:07,150 --> 00:12:08,480
But I won't hurt anyone.

122
00:12:11,870 --> 00:12:13,600
The woman who died today...

123
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:16,040
was quite pretty.

124
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:20,910
But you killed her anyway.

125
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:25,480
I like you now,

126
00:12:26,590 --> 00:12:28,590
but that doesn't mean I always will.

127
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:31,840
If I stop liking you someday,

128
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:34,600
I might kill you.

129
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:40,370
Why are you NBIS people
always shooting and killing?

130
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:42,960
To save this country,

131
00:12:44,090 --> 00:12:45,890
someone has to die along the way.

132
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:49,030
Unless...

133
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:52,670
you become mine.

134
00:12:54,030 --> 00:12:54,840
Impossible.

135
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:03,370
Pretend to be my husband...

136
00:13:05,630 --> 00:13:06,710
be my cover.

137
00:13:08,630 --> 00:13:10,430
I don't think that's necessary.

138
00:13:10,480 --> 00:13:11,210
Chen Kailai,

139
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:13,270
you're destined to be my partner.

140
00:13:13,270 --> 00:13:14,600
There's no escaping it.

141
00:13:17,670 --> 00:13:18,750
Better be careful,

142
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:21,320
given the kind of work you do.

143
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:24,650
You care about me that much?

144
00:13:25,840 --> 00:13:28,040
I'm afraid you'll drag me down with you.

145
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:30,310
Then treat me to wontons
every day from now on,

146
00:13:30,310 --> 00:13:31,710
and I'll spare your life!

147
00:14:57,570 --> 00:15:00,710
[Xiaoxian]

148
00:14:58,770 --> 00:15:00,770
The person who betrayed you is dead.

149
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:03,480
I slit her throat myself.

150
00:15:05,090 --> 00:15:06,920
You slit Suzuki's throat too?

151
00:15:07,570 --> 00:15:08,830
That really wasn't me.

152
00:15:10,930 --> 00:15:12,590
God couldn't stand it anymore

153
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:15,600
and decided to claim his life.

154
00:15:27,010 --> 00:15:28,130
Weren't you afraid

155
00:15:28,760 --> 00:15:31,760
that I might've actually
pulled the trigger that day?

156
00:15:34,530 --> 00:15:35,610
I still regret

157
00:15:36,270 --> 00:15:38,330
handing over the document so easily—

158
00:15:39,010 --> 00:15:41,670
I should've squeezed a fortune
out of you first.

159
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:43,490
You managed to get

160
00:15:43,490 --> 00:15:46,550
the Japanese document out
while fleeing for your life.

161
00:15:46,680 --> 00:15:48,480
I should've realized right then

162
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:51,200
that you were the real God of Wealth.

163
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:55,010
Don't I look like a dance hostess?

164
00:15:55,010 --> 00:15:55,650
You do.

165
00:15:56,850 --> 00:15:59,110
That's why you hid your identity so well.

166
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:03,510
Since you'd been keeping an eye
on Suzuki for so long,

167
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:06,200
you could've taken the document yourself.

168
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:08,320
Why did you need me?

169
00:16:13,830 --> 00:16:14,730
The Japanese will soon

170
00:16:14,730 --> 00:16:16,680
set up a research institute in Shanghai.

171
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:18,040
After you get the document,

172
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:19,520
your mission in Hangzhou will be over.

173
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:20,780
Leave for Shanghai immediately,

174
00:16:20,780 --> 00:16:21,510
get settled,

175
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:24,790
and continue looking for clues
about Project Slumber.

176
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:27,410
I stole the intelligence from Suzuki,

177
00:16:28,350 --> 00:16:30,590
so the Japanese were bound to
come looking for me.

178
00:16:30,590 --> 00:16:33,720
Having you take the document away
was the safest option.

179
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:38,280
How did you and that Chen guy

180
00:16:38,280 --> 00:16:39,680
get tangled up together?

181
00:16:43,730 --> 00:16:44,730
We just happened

182
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:47,120
to meet at the train station.

183
00:16:47,730 --> 00:16:48,440
Tell me,

184
00:16:49,520 --> 00:16:51,050
is this what they call fate?

185
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:07,200
I think it sounds more like something
you arranged yourself.

186
00:17:08,089 --> 00:17:09,369
You can put it that way.

187
00:17:11,099 --> 00:17:12,500
He was going to Shanghai,

188
00:17:13,089 --> 00:17:14,290
and so was I.

189
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:17,849
I needed a cover identity,

190
00:17:19,290 --> 00:17:21,510
so I took him along
to seek refuge with Xiaoxian.

191
00:17:21,510 --> 00:17:24,640
[Tomb of the Late Yang Xiaoxian]

192
00:17:22,810 --> 00:17:25,470
As it happened, he wanted to
open a photo studio,

193
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:28,520
and I needed to settle down
near the bathhouse.

194
00:17:29,570 --> 00:17:30,970
So I used that as a pretext

195
00:17:31,530 --> 00:17:32,790
and opened one myself.

196
00:17:34,370 --> 00:17:35,240
At every turn,

197
00:17:35,610 --> 00:17:38,010
he unwittingly played right into my hands.

198
00:17:38,610 --> 00:17:40,410
That's what you'd call destiny.

199
00:17:45,850 --> 00:17:47,090
In our line of work,

200
00:17:47,860 --> 00:17:50,060
falling for someone is very dangerous.

201
00:17:54,750 --> 00:17:55,990
That's my business.

202
00:17:59,190 --> 00:18:01,250
You heard what that traitor said too.

203
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:03,090
Ou Yang.

204
00:18:04,440 --> 00:18:05,240
Find her,

205
00:18:06,140 --> 00:18:09,320
and we might finally uncover the secret
behind Project Slumber.

206
00:18:09,320 --> 00:18:09,920
Got it.

207
00:18:11,570 --> 00:18:13,100
Chen is Du Huangqiao's man.

208
00:18:14,050 --> 00:18:14,810
Be careful.

209
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:18,370
You never know how things will turn out.

210
00:18:18,370 --> 00:18:19,430
Who can really tell

211
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:21,570
friend from foe?

212
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:29,920
There was a shootout at MGM yesterday.

213
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:31,970
Sachiko is dead.

214
00:18:33,650 --> 00:18:35,130
The Hurricane Team did it.

215
00:18:37,610 --> 00:18:40,160
It wouldn't matter
if she were the only one who died.

216
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,760
But the Japanese military officer with her

217
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:42,620
was killed too.

218
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:48,600
That's always been
the Hurricane Team's way of doing things.

219
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:50,410
You can only say he was unlucky.

220
00:18:54,810 --> 00:18:56,640
What, am I supposed to tell Kagesa

221
00:18:56,640 --> 00:18:58,040
that he was just unlucky?

222
00:19:02,960 --> 00:19:03,610
Director,

223
00:19:04,530 --> 00:19:06,190
please give me some more time.

224
00:19:06,990 --> 00:19:08,990
The Hurricane Team or God of Wealth—

225
00:19:09,500 --> 00:19:10,530
I'll catch them all for you.

226
00:19:10,530 --> 00:19:13,440
I need to give Kagesa
an explanation right now.

227
00:19:17,760 --> 00:19:18,680
That's easy.

228
00:19:20,530 --> 00:19:22,530
With so many dance hostesses at MGM,

229
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:24,200
any one of them

230
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:26,820
could be from the Hurricane Team.

231
00:19:27,090 --> 00:19:27,890
Let's do that.

232
00:19:55,530 --> 00:19:56,570
As you wanted,

233
00:19:57,130 --> 00:19:59,930
Chen Kailai has officially
become Broken Bridge.

234
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:03,920
We'll need his help with the work ahead.

235
00:20:04,260 --> 00:20:05,920
You'll be his liaison for now.

236
00:20:06,470 --> 00:20:07,150
Okay.

237
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:11,780
Ou Yang's father is Ou Gengsheng.

238
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:14,370
He's been doing business
in Japan for years

239
00:20:14,370 --> 00:20:16,890
and has already
taken Japanese citizenship.

240
00:20:16,890 --> 00:20:19,090
Kagesa probably doesn't
want to offend him,

241
00:20:19,090 --> 00:20:21,530
but he's also afraid Ou Yang
might leak their secrets,

242
00:20:21,530 --> 00:20:22,890
so he's hidden her away.

243
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:29,070
Sending someone into the Plum Blossom Agency
to find her is too risky.

244
00:20:29,070 --> 00:20:30,760
Then think of a less risky way.

245
00:20:32,890 --> 00:20:34,150
That guy named Ishida.

246
00:20:34,890 --> 00:20:36,620
He might know her whereabouts.

247
00:20:48,810 --> 00:20:49,610
Mr. Zhao.

248
00:20:49,850 --> 00:20:51,920
Mr. Chen, take some photos for me.

249
00:20:55,050 --> 00:20:56,310
Business or personal?

250
00:20:57,370 --> 00:20:58,970
Like you don't already know.

251
00:20:59,960 --> 00:21:02,400
Mr. Zhao, first the official car
for your own errands,

252
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:04,310
and now you won't even
leave the photographer alone?

253
00:21:04,310 --> 00:21:06,040
Isn't that a little too brazen?

254
00:21:06,070 --> 00:21:06,800
Look here!

255
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:09,890
Relax a bit.

256
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:12,200
Good. You look great when you smile.

257
00:21:13,850 --> 00:21:16,290
I never imagined
Jinbao was actually God of Wealth.

258
00:21:16,290 --> 00:21:17,720
Living under the same roof as her,

259
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:18,920
you must be careful.

260
00:21:19,840 --> 00:21:20,910
She won't kill me.

261
00:21:21,790 --> 00:21:23,100
She's not Jinbao anymore.

262
00:21:23,100 --> 00:21:24,230
She's God of Wealth.

263
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:26,680
Good! Very beautiful!

264
00:21:26,680 --> 00:21:27,650
Hold it!

265
00:21:32,350 --> 00:21:33,950
You have a mission coming up.

266
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:37,700
Hoshino's daughter's birthday
is in a few days.

267
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:39,950
They're holding a birthday party at home.

268
00:21:39,950 --> 00:21:41,080
Su Men will be there.

269
00:21:42,090 --> 00:21:42,840
It's a birthday party,

270
00:21:42,840 --> 00:21:45,300
so they'll definitely need a photographer.

271
00:21:48,150 --> 00:21:49,480
What do you need me to do?

272
00:21:50,050 --> 00:21:51,180
Get close to Ishida.

273
00:21:52,560 --> 00:21:53,280
Ishida?

274
00:21:53,450 --> 00:21:54,050
Yes.

275
00:21:54,290 --> 00:21:56,890
The assistant
who's always by Hoshino's side.

276
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:58,570
We've received intelligence

277
00:21:58,570 --> 00:22:00,100
that Ou Yang is still alive.

278
00:22:00,370 --> 00:22:01,610
Find a way to use Ishida

279
00:22:01,610 --> 00:22:03,410
to learn Ou Yang's whereabouts.

280
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:07,090
Got it.

281
00:22:10,920 --> 00:22:11,760
This is your first mission

282
00:22:11,760 --> 00:22:13,370
as Broken Bridge.

283
00:22:14,680 --> 00:22:16,480
Make sure you protect yourself.

284
00:22:16,570 --> 00:22:17,760
If you run into danger,

285
00:22:17,760 --> 00:22:19,890
keep your cover intact above all else.

286
00:22:20,610 --> 00:22:22,110
A failed mission isn't scary—

287
00:22:22,110 --> 00:22:23,280
being exposed is.

288
00:22:27,160 --> 00:22:28,560
I have one more question.

289
00:22:30,330 --> 00:22:32,610
What if Su Men doesn't take me along?

290
00:22:33,140 --> 00:22:35,270
Come on. Come with me to get some honey.

291
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:37,600
Alright, let's take a break!

292
00:22:38,050 --> 00:22:39,160
Thank you.

293
00:22:39,480 --> 00:22:41,610
How old is Sakura?

294
00:22:41,670 --> 00:22:42,560
She's 12 now.

295
00:22:42,920 --> 00:22:43,680
Sakura.

296
00:22:44,490 --> 00:22:45,490
Happy birthday.

297
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:47,400
This is a present for you.

298
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:49,490
Quick, say thank you to Auntie.

299
00:22:50,220 --> 00:22:51,280
Thank you, Auntie.

300
00:23:03,780 --> 00:23:04,570
Mr. Hoshino.

301
00:23:05,490 --> 00:23:07,120
May I have a word with you?

302
00:23:18,850 --> 00:23:21,090
Mr. Hoshino, I want to resign.

303
00:23:26,050 --> 00:23:26,780
Come with me.

304
00:23:42,790 --> 00:23:44,070
You want to resign?

305
00:23:46,090 --> 00:23:48,720
Sorry to disappoint you, Mr. Hoshino.

306
00:23:50,850 --> 00:23:52,910
It's because of that woman, isn't it?

307
00:24:06,130 --> 00:24:07,610
I warned you—

308
00:24:08,330 --> 00:24:10,330
stay away from those Chinese women.

309
00:24:10,850 --> 00:24:13,290
They'll only make you lose your resolve.

310
00:24:15,650 --> 00:24:16,380
Mr. Hoshino.

311
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:21,090
Is it really that I've lost my resolve,

312
00:24:22,370 --> 00:24:24,650
or are we simply doing something wrong?

313
00:24:26,440 --> 00:24:29,330
You're questioning
the decisions of our country?

314
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:33,370
Back home,

315
00:24:34,460 --> 00:24:36,920
I felt these things
were far removed from me.

316
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:40,680
But now that I'm in China,

317
00:24:41,570 --> 00:24:42,900
standing on their land,

318
00:24:43,050 --> 00:24:44,710
getting to know their people—

319
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:47,000
they're just like us,

320
00:24:47,200 --> 00:24:49,060
living, breathing human beings!

321
00:24:49,450 --> 00:24:50,450
Coward!

322
00:24:51,810 --> 00:24:53,680
Everything we do

323
00:24:54,130 --> 00:24:56,730
is for the rejuvenation
of the Empire of Japan!

324
00:24:58,240 --> 00:24:59,570
I'm sorry, Mr. Hoshino.

325
00:25:01,490 --> 00:25:05,250
I'll still fight for our country
when I get back.

326
00:25:10,470 --> 00:25:11,230
Wait!

327
00:25:40,090 --> 00:25:40,960
Konnichiwa.

328
00:25:42,480 --> 00:25:43,160
Ni Hao.

329
00:25:43,480 --> 00:25:44,480
It's been a while.

330
00:25:45,280 --> 00:25:47,210
Mr. Chen, you speak some Japanese?

331
00:25:48,090 --> 00:25:49,440
I've only just started learning.

332
00:25:49,440 --> 00:25:51,440
I'm still too nervous to speak much.

333
00:25:51,440 --> 00:25:53,240
I've been studying Chinese too.

334
00:25:54,240 --> 00:25:56,770
Then perhaps we can
hone our skills together.

335
00:25:57,860 --> 00:25:58,750
Hone?

336
00:25:59,590 --> 00:26:02,120
It means...
practicing together to improve.

337
00:26:04,810 --> 00:26:05,530
Okay.

338
00:26:07,440 --> 00:26:08,290
However...

339
00:26:08,890 --> 00:26:09,890
I'm really sorry.

340
00:26:11,200 --> 00:26:12,530
I'm going back to Japan.

341
00:26:13,290 --> 00:26:14,050
Really?

342
00:26:14,620 --> 00:26:15,350
So suddenly?

343
00:26:16,570 --> 00:26:18,900
I've been thinking about it for some time.

344
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:21,530
Thank you.

345
00:26:26,060 --> 00:26:27,290
Before you leave,

346
00:26:28,040 --> 00:26:29,440
let me treat you to a meal.

347
00:26:30,900 --> 00:26:32,430
I hope I'll have the chance.

348
00:26:37,160 --> 00:26:38,090
Sorry, Mr. Chen.

349
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:39,570
I'm busy today.

350
00:26:40,480 --> 00:26:41,610
I'll be leaving now.

351
00:27:38,480 --> 00:27:39,940
Telegram from Chongqing.

352
00:27:40,010 --> 00:27:42,610
The Hurricane Team is
also looking for Ou Yang.

353
00:27:46,240 --> 00:27:47,840
Their intelligence network

354
00:27:48,330 --> 00:27:49,990
is pretty well-informed too.

355
00:27:55,810 --> 00:27:58,130
Please deliver this
to Mr. Ishida Shota for me.

356
00:27:58,130 --> 00:28:00,060
Tell him it's from Mr. Chen.

357
00:28:00,130 --> 00:28:00,780
Okay.

358
00:28:04,320 --> 00:28:06,360
[Dream of the Red Chamber]

359
00:28:21,400 --> 00:28:23,200
"To Mr. Ishida Shota.

360
00:28:23,480 --> 00:28:25,480
A gift to commemorate our friendship.

361
00:28:25,480 --> 00:28:28,140
May your days ahead
be peaceful and prosperous.

362
00:28:28,610 --> 00:28:31,190
Chen Kailai, 31st Year
of the Republic of China,

363
00:28:31,190 --> 00:28:32,520
at Fulai Photo Studio."

364
00:28:39,610 --> 00:28:40,820
Come on, sir. Be careful.

365
00:28:40,820 --> 00:28:41,500
Thank you.

366
00:28:48,100 --> 00:28:49,530
Excuse me.

367
00:28:53,130 --> 00:28:53,650
Hello.

368
00:28:53,920 --> 00:28:56,290
Are you here to
take photos or pick up prints?

369
00:28:56,290 --> 00:28:56,850
Neither.

370
00:28:58,130 --> 00:28:59,530
I'm looking for your boss.

371
00:28:59,530 --> 00:29:00,290
Oh, my boss.

372
00:29:00,680 --> 00:29:01,400
Sis!

373
00:29:03,290 --> 00:29:04,160
For God's sake!

374
00:29:04,450 --> 00:29:05,980
Someone is looking for you.

375
00:29:11,200 --> 00:29:11,810
Sorry.

376
00:29:12,810 --> 00:29:14,670
I must've come to the wrong place.

377
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:15,760
Sir,

378
00:29:16,330 --> 00:29:18,730
I assume you're looking for
the other boss.

379
00:29:20,440 --> 00:29:21,290
Chen Kailai?

380
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:24,760
I'm Jinbao.

381
00:29:25,090 --> 00:29:27,050
Mr. Chen's friend is my friend.

382
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:30,960
My name is Ishida Shota.

383
00:29:32,050 --> 00:29:33,310
He should be back soon.

384
00:29:33,370 --> 00:29:34,970
Come on, have a seat over here.

385
00:29:34,970 --> 00:29:35,570
Please.

386
00:29:50,290 --> 00:29:51,130
Handsome,

387
00:29:52,130 --> 00:29:53,260
what brings you here

388
00:29:53,740 --> 00:29:54,820
to see him?

389
00:29:58,810 --> 00:30:00,410
I've brought him some books.

390
00:30:03,240 --> 00:30:04,800
Are you learning Chinese,

391
00:30:04,900 --> 00:30:06,430
or is he learning Japanese?

392
00:30:08,720 --> 00:30:10,480
We hone each other's skills.

393
00:30:11,610 --> 00:30:13,270
Then you could ask me for help.

394
00:30:14,390 --> 00:30:16,430
I'm a pretty good teacher too.

395
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:19,730
Thank you for the offer.

396
00:30:20,680 --> 00:30:21,480
But...

397
00:30:23,400 --> 00:30:25,000
it has to be Mr. Chen.

398
00:30:26,030 --> 00:30:27,990
I'm more interested in Mr. Chen.

399
00:30:31,440 --> 00:30:32,200
Sorry.

400
00:30:32,810 --> 00:30:34,810
I may not have said that quite right.

401
00:30:37,480 --> 00:30:38,610
You like him a lot?

402
00:30:48,920 --> 00:30:49,890
Mr. Ishida?

403
00:30:50,360 --> 00:30:51,010
Mr. Chen.

404
00:30:51,280 --> 00:30:53,340
I'm entertaining your guest for you.

405
00:30:53,840 --> 00:30:55,370
Ms. Jin is very hospitable.

406
00:30:56,160 --> 00:30:58,420
Thank you for your hospitality, Ms. Jin.

407
00:30:58,810 --> 00:30:59,450
But

408
00:30:59,470 --> 00:31:00,800
we should get going now.

409
00:31:00,810 --> 00:31:02,160
Okay, okay, let's go.

410
00:31:02,360 --> 00:31:03,850
Were you teasing him?

411
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:04,890
Seriously.

412
00:31:05,240 --> 00:31:06,200
Don't go.

413
00:31:21,160 --> 00:31:24,050
These are all the members
of Hoshino's research group.

414
00:31:24,050 --> 00:31:25,710
The girl on the left is Ou Yang.

415
00:31:40,530 --> 00:31:42,130
I've booked the boat ticket.

416
00:31:42,330 --> 00:31:43,590
I'm leaving next week.

417
00:31:48,050 --> 00:31:49,050
These are for you,

418
00:31:49,370 --> 00:31:50,300
in return.

419
00:31:52,200 --> 00:31:54,480
I hope they help you learn Japanese.

420
00:31:56,000 --> 00:31:56,670
Thank you.

421
00:31:57,090 --> 00:31:58,160
I'll study hard.

422
00:32:02,370 --> 00:32:03,370
Try the food here.

423
00:32:03,800 --> 00:32:07,130
See if it's as good as the place
your classmate recommended.

424
00:32:07,760 --> 00:32:09,720
The food doesn't matter.

425
00:32:10,480 --> 00:32:13,140
Your friendship means more to me
than anything.

426
00:32:13,610 --> 00:32:15,090
Then I should give you a proper

427
00:32:15,090 --> 00:32:16,090
send-off.

428
00:32:20,290 --> 00:32:20,960
Oh,

429
00:32:21,890 --> 00:32:23,950
should we invite your classmate too?

430
00:32:23,960 --> 00:32:25,820
We could all have a meal together.

431
00:32:29,760 --> 00:32:30,760
She won't come.

432
00:32:31,570 --> 00:32:32,370
Why?

433
00:32:34,090 --> 00:32:34,890
She's sick.

434
00:32:36,680 --> 00:32:37,290
Sick?

435
00:32:38,570 --> 00:32:40,370
Then aren't you going to see her?

436
00:32:43,740 --> 00:32:44,540
Forget it.

437
00:32:48,680 --> 00:32:49,810
I just think

438
00:32:50,810 --> 00:32:52,200
since you like her,

439
00:32:52,370 --> 00:32:53,770
you should fight for her.

440
00:32:54,200 --> 00:32:55,390
Missing your chance now

441
00:32:55,390 --> 00:32:57,190
could become a lifelong regret.

442
00:32:58,200 --> 00:32:59,720
I already tried.

443
00:33:01,540 --> 00:33:03,400
Unfortunately, she rejected me.

444
00:33:07,090 --> 00:33:09,020
Her heart belongs to someone else.

445
00:33:11,450 --> 00:33:14,110
If you can't be lovers,
you can still be friends.

446
00:33:18,240 --> 00:33:20,970
But I don't think
I can even be her friend anymore.

447
00:33:24,570 --> 00:33:26,760
If you leave without saying a word,

448
00:33:27,310 --> 00:33:29,510
then you really aren't much of a friend.

449
00:33:32,200 --> 00:33:34,810
Do I really still have the right
to see her?

450
00:33:36,190 --> 00:33:37,120
Although I don't know

451
00:33:37,120 --> 00:33:39,320
what exactly happened between you two,

452
00:33:40,440 --> 00:33:41,900
you still can't let her go.

453
00:33:42,200 --> 00:33:43,480
Since you still care about her,

454
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:46,540
you need to settle this between you,
one way or another.

455
00:33:52,680 --> 00:33:53,650
You're right.

456
00:33:56,480 --> 00:33:57,440
Before leaving,

457
00:33:58,240 --> 00:34:00,300
I really should see her one more time.

458
00:34:01,810 --> 00:34:02,400
Come on.

459
00:34:02,680 --> 00:34:03,650
Let's drink. Come on.

460
00:34:03,650 --> 00:34:04,980
Stop thinking about it.

461
00:35:05,830 --> 00:35:06,670
Another one.

462
00:35:07,760 --> 00:35:08,880
Another one.

463
00:35:10,310 --> 00:35:11,740
Another one.

464
00:35:14,530 --> 00:35:16,130
Another one...

465
00:35:23,390 --> 00:35:24,260
I'm sorry.

466
00:35:29,200 --> 00:35:29,970
I'm sorry...

467
00:35:30,360 --> 00:35:31,930
I'm sorry, Ou Yang.

468
00:35:34,450 --> 00:35:35,490
I'm sorry...

469
00:35:36,390 --> 00:35:37,660
I'm sorry, Ou Yang.

470
00:35:41,240 --> 00:35:42,720
I've failed her.

471
00:35:46,610 --> 00:35:47,760
I'm sorry.

472
00:35:57,260 --> 00:35:58,470
I'm sorry.

473
00:37:03,840 --> 00:37:04,440
This is it.

474
00:37:04,760 --> 00:37:05,450
Alright.

475
00:37:07,650 --> 00:37:08,720
Here. Thank you.

476
00:37:08,980 --> 00:37:09,570
Thank you.

477
00:37:09,570 --> 00:37:10,840
One bowl of wontons, please.

478
00:37:10,840 --> 00:37:12,440
Coming right up. Have a seat.

479
00:37:16,650 --> 00:37:18,450
Before Ishida leaves Shanghai,

480
00:37:18,930 --> 00:37:20,990
he should go see Ou Yang one more time.

481
00:37:21,240 --> 00:37:24,040
You can get him to see Ou Yang
with just a few drinks?

482
00:37:26,650 --> 00:37:28,710
Ishida is a man who follows his heart.

483
00:37:29,410 --> 00:37:31,240
He hasn't let go of Ou Yang.

484
00:37:32,320 --> 00:37:33,160
And

485
00:37:33,930 --> 00:37:36,390
it seems like he did Ou Yang wrong
in some way.

486
00:37:36,970 --> 00:37:37,680
What is it?

487
00:37:37,930 --> 00:37:38,730
He didn't say.

488
00:37:39,320 --> 00:37:40,050
He was drunk

489
00:37:40,450 --> 00:37:41,850
and didn't say anything.

490
00:37:48,300 --> 00:37:49,050
Good job.

491
00:37:51,500 --> 00:37:53,760
But don't get too pleased with yourself.

492
00:37:54,650 --> 00:37:55,500
Shanghai...

493
00:37:55,500 --> 00:37:57,230
Is not an easy place to survive.

494
00:38:00,140 --> 00:38:00,870
By the way...

495
00:38:02,420 --> 00:38:03,780
you might need this.

496
00:38:09,690 --> 00:38:13,890
I took those photos when I went to
Hoshino's house for the banquet last time.

497
00:38:18,020 --> 00:38:19,080
A little thank you.

498
00:38:21,530 --> 00:38:22,790
Your wontons are on me.

499
00:38:37,300 --> 00:38:39,960
Why did you suddenly
think of making me wontons?

500
00:38:40,650 --> 00:38:42,820
I always keep my word.

501
00:38:45,500 --> 00:38:47,900
Did you do something
you feel guilty about?

502
00:38:50,020 --> 00:38:52,080
Why do I feel like you're a bit touchy?

503
00:38:52,860 --> 00:38:54,650
I just made this bowl of wontons for you.

504
00:38:54,650 --> 00:38:55,340
Want it?

505
00:38:56,600 --> 00:38:57,250
No!

506
00:39:00,780 --> 00:39:02,200
Last time, to save me,

507
00:39:02,300 --> 00:39:03,830
you gave Shasha 5,000 yuan.

508
00:39:04,730 --> 00:39:06,990
I got the money back from Cang Guanglian.

509
00:39:07,090 --> 00:39:07,730
Want it?

510
00:39:15,910 --> 00:39:18,580
Having connections really
does make a difference.

511
00:39:18,580 --> 00:39:21,910
I'd say you're getting pretty comfortable
being a traitor.

512
00:39:25,940 --> 00:39:27,340
Let me ask you something.

513
00:39:28,410 --> 00:39:31,070
What exactly is
your relationship with Ishida?

514
00:39:31,300 --> 00:39:31,940
Friends.

515
00:39:33,430 --> 00:39:34,560
How did you meet him?

516
00:39:35,530 --> 00:39:37,780
I saved him at the racecourse last time.

517
00:39:38,990 --> 00:39:41,450
Has he ever mentioned
his girlfriend to you?

518
00:39:44,610 --> 00:39:47,410
I'm starting to think
you have an ulterior motive.

519
00:39:48,570 --> 00:39:50,050
He has a girlfriend? Who?

520
00:39:51,130 --> 00:39:52,420
A Chinese woman.

521
00:39:54,340 --> 00:39:55,400
Her name is Ou Yang.

522
00:39:56,900 --> 00:39:57,900
Tell me honestly.

523
00:39:58,300 --> 00:39:59,050
Don't lie.

524
00:39:59,510 --> 00:40:01,030
I can tell at a glance.

525
00:40:04,730 --> 00:40:06,330
Not his girlfriend, I think.

526
00:40:07,610 --> 00:40:09,870
He does have feelings for a Chinese girl.

527
00:40:10,380 --> 00:40:12,110
She was his classmate in Japan.

528
00:40:13,380 --> 00:40:15,510
He's learning Chinese because of her.

529
00:40:16,250 --> 00:40:17,580
Are they still in touch?

530
00:40:18,170 --> 00:40:19,170
I don't think so.

531
00:40:20,230 --> 00:40:21,500
So he's heartbroken

532
00:40:21,530 --> 00:40:23,130
and plans to return to Japan.

533
00:40:23,940 --> 00:40:26,340
Going home just because he's heartbroken?

534
00:40:26,770 --> 00:40:27,970
Maybe he's homesick.

535
00:40:30,020 --> 00:40:32,550
Then he'll never
accomplish anything great.

536
00:40:35,460 --> 00:40:38,460
Aren't family and love
among the great things in life?

537
00:40:40,690 --> 00:40:42,020
Not in times like these.

538
00:40:42,900 --> 00:40:45,050
If that's how you see it, I'm relieved.

539
00:40:45,830 --> 00:40:47,630
To you, everything is a big deal.

540
00:40:50,980 --> 00:40:51,790
Remember—

541
00:40:52,860 --> 00:40:54,380
you must report any news

542
00:40:54,380 --> 00:40:56,040
about Ishida to me at any time.

543
00:40:56,140 --> 00:40:57,180
Why should I?

544
00:40:57,200 --> 00:40:58,660
I'm not your subordinate.

545
00:40:59,130 --> 00:41:00,650
You can be mine.

546
00:41:05,570 --> 00:41:06,650
I think I'll pass.

547
00:41:07,820 --> 00:41:09,620
I'd like to live a few more years.

548
00:41:21,430 --> 00:41:22,950
Flowers!

549
00:41:23,820 --> 00:41:25,340
Flowers!

550
00:41:26,170 --> 00:41:26,970
Excuse me.

551
00:41:27,530 --> 00:41:28,590
I'd like a bouquet.

552
00:41:28,740 --> 00:41:29,420
How much?

553
00:41:29,600 --> 00:41:30,370
Thirty yuan.

554
00:41:33,700 --> 00:41:34,590
Here you go.

555
00:41:34,690 --> 00:41:35,330
Thank you.

556
00:41:37,700 --> 00:41:38,900
Need a rickshaw, sir?

557
00:41:39,860 --> 00:41:40,480
Are you free?

558
00:41:40,480 --> 00:41:41,080
Of course.

559
00:41:43,050 --> 00:41:43,570
Please.

560
00:41:43,600 --> 00:41:44,040
Okay.

561
00:41:44,680 --> 00:41:45,280
Where to?

562
00:41:45,810 --> 00:41:47,030
I'm going to Fumin Hospital.

563
00:41:47,030 --> 00:41:48,550
Okay. Sit tight.

564
00:41:49,140 --> 00:41:50,540
Come on, coming through!

565
00:41:59,820 --> 00:42:00,490
Thank you.

566
00:42:06,440 --> 00:42:09,070
[Fumin Hospital]

567
00:42:13,460 --> 00:42:14,560
[Outpatient Department; Inpatient Ward]

568
00:42:43,830 --> 00:42:45,890
Ishida went to Fumin Hospital today.

569
00:42:46,670 --> 00:42:48,730
I suspect Ou Yang is being held there.

570
00:42:49,270 --> 00:42:50,200
Fumin Hospital.

571
00:42:51,820 --> 00:42:53,680
That's a Japanese-run hospital.

572
00:42:54,570 --> 00:42:56,430
The security there is very tight.

573
00:42:58,210 --> 00:43:00,740
We need to send someone in
to scope things out.

574
00:43:01,500 --> 00:43:02,460
Do you have someone in mind?
